    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34-a3">

                <pb facs="0134" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg38"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 75.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. McKinley &amp;
                            Gottlieb to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Yours of January 28, 1898, received.
                    According to instructions we herewith forward certified copies of citizenship of
                    the father of Ignatz Gutman, and also affidavits that said Ignatz Gutman came to
                    this country as a minor and is a citizen of the United States.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d34-f1"/></p>
                <p>We kindly ask you to investigate this matter and to demand the release of said
                    Ignatz Gutman from the Hungarian army, where he is serving.</p>
                <p>A reply awaiting, we are, yours, most respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McKinley &amp; Gottlieb.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d34-f1" n="1" xml:id="d34-f1-content">
                <p>Inclosures not printed.</p>
